const PRIVACY = "This Policy explains how the mobile AI video creator operated by Felix Lindner processes information when you generate videos, use AI Chat, manage your history, or purchase a subscription. Some information is processed by external AI and subscription service providers, even though the App does not use its own backend.\n\n## Who operates the App\n\nThe application (the “App”) is operated by Felix Lindner, an individual based in Germany (“we,” “us,” or “our”). Felix Lindner is the point of contact for questions about this Policy and, to the extent applicable, the controller of personal data processed in connection with operating the App. The Higgsfield brand is used under authorization; this does not make Higgsfield Inc. the operator of this App.\n\n## Information involved in your use of the App\n\nContent you choose to provide. Text prompts, generation instructions, reference images (including multiple images), images attached to AI Chat, chat messages and relevant chat context are processed to provide the features you request. Generated videos and responses are returned for display and optional saving or sharing. The App does not require you to upload an existing video file as input for the described AI features.\n\nLocal activity and preferences. Your generation history, favorites, saved prompts and other in-app state may be stored on your device so you can revisit, recreate, or delete results. These local records are not stored on a proprietary backend operated by us.\n\nCamera and photo saving. With your permission, the App can use your camera to capture images for creation or chat features. The Photos “Add Only” permission allows the App to save content to your photo library; it does not, by itself, grant access to browse your entire photo library. You control whether to capture, attach, export, or save content.\n\nSubscriptions and support. If you subscribe, Apple handles billing and may make subscription status and transaction information available to the App and its subscription-management provider, Apphud. If you contact us by email, we receive the details you voluntarily provide in that message.\n\n## AI providers and external processing\n\nThe App uses AI services provided by fal.ai and OpenAI. Depending on the feature, prompts, instructions, reference images, image attachments, and chat content or context are sent to the relevant provider for AI processing and generation. Generated responses and videos are delivered back to the App. These transfers are necessary to operate the requested text-to-video, image-to-video, and AI Chat features.\n\nWe do not operate an independent application backend to store these submissions. However, the AI providers may process and retain inputs, outputs, related technical information and operational logs on their own infrastructure, under their respective terms and privacy practices. We cannot promise immediate deletion or a fixed retention period on those systems. When you connect to their services, they may also receive technical connection information, such as an IP address, as part of ordinary network operations.\n\n## Subscription processing through Apphud and Apple\n\nThe App uses ApphudSDK to manage subscriptions and paid entitlements. Apphud may process subscription status, purchase-related events, an Apphud-specific user identifier, and, depending on device and SDK configuration, identifiers such as Apple’s Identifier for Vendor (IDFV) or related technical information. Apple processes payments, purchase history, and Apple Account information under its own privacy terms. We do not receive your full payment-card number from Apple.\n\nThe App has no advertising functionality, does not integrate a separate analytics SDK, Firebase, or a dedicated crash-reporting service, and does not use personal data for cross-app advertising tracking. Subscription-related event processing by Apphud should not be interpreted as an assertion that no data is processed by third-party SDKs.\n\n## Why information is processed and legal grounds\n\n- To provide the features you request, including video generation, AI Chat, local history, exports, and subscription access (performance of a contract, where applicable).\n- To respond to support requests and handle technical or payment-related questions (performance of a contract and/or legitimate interests in providing customer support).\n- To maintain service reliability, prevent misuse, and protect legal rights, as reasonably necessary (legitimate interests and, where applicable, legal obligations).\n- To comply with applicable legal requirements, such as consumer, tax, or regulatory obligations (legal obligations).\n\nWhere consent is legally required for a specific activity, we will rely on consent and provide the applicable choices. Operating-system permission prompts are managed through your device settings and can be changed there.\n\n## Storage, retention, and deletion\n\nIn-app history and favorites are kept locally unless you remove them or uninstall the App. You can use available in-app controls to delete your history or generation results. Deleting a local entry does not necessarily delete a video you previously saved to Photos, shared with another app, or otherwise exported.\n\nDeletion within the App does not automatically ensure deletion of information previously processed by fal.ai, OpenAI, Apple, or Apphud. Their applicable retention periods and deletion procedures may differ. We do not control the retention practices of those providers and cannot guarantee removal from their systems through an in-app deletion action. Support emails may be retained as reasonably necessary to respond, maintain records, or meet legal obligations.\n\n## Disclosure and international data transfers\n\nRelevant information may be made available to fal.ai and OpenAI for AI features, Apphud and Apple for subscription services, and recipients you select when you share or export content. We do not offer public posting or user-to-user messaging within the App. Providers may process information outside Germany or the European Economic Area, including in the United States; applicable transfer protections and provider practices depend on the service and circumstances.\n\n## Your choices and privacy rights\n\nYou can choose not to submit particular prompts or images, manage camera and photo permissions in device settings, and delete available locally stored history or results. You may also be able to manage or delete content held by external providers under their policies.\n\nWhere the GDPR or other privacy law applies, you may have rights to request access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, or to object to certain processing, and to withdraw consent where processing relies on it. You may also lodge a complaint with a competent data protection supervisory authority. To exercise rights relating to data we control, email the address below. We will assist within the limits of our access to data and applicable law; requests concerning provider-held data may need to be directed to the relevant provider.\n\n## Security, children, and changes\n\nWe use the platform and service mechanisms available to operate the App, but no transmission or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure. Please avoid submitting sensitive, confidential, or third-party personal material unless you have the necessary rights and are comfortable with the processing described here. The App does not support generation of explicit adult (18+) content; this restriction does not establish that all AI-generated content will be suitable for every age.\n\nWe may update this Policy when the App, providers, or legal requirements change. The updated version will show a revised effective date and will be made available through the App or another appropriate channel.\n\n## Contact\n\nFor privacy questions or requests relating to this App, please contact:\n\nFelix Lindner\nPrierosser Str. 45, 12357 Berlin, Germany\nEmail: felix@lindnerapp.click";

const TERMS = "These Terms govern access to and use of the mobile AI video creator operated by Felix Lindner. The App provides AI video generation, AI Chat, prompt inspiration, local history and subscription-based features. Please read these Terms together with the Privacy Policy before using the App.\n\n## Operator and acceptance\n\nThe App is offered by Felix Lindner, Prierosser Str. 45, 12357 Berlin, Germany (“Operator,” “we,” “us,” or “our”). By downloading, accessing, or using the App, you agree to these Terms to the extent permitted by applicable law. If you do not agree, please do not use the App. If you are under the age required to agree to these Terms independently in your jurisdiction, you must have appropriate parental or guardian permission.\n\n## Features and availability\n\nThe App can generate AI videos from text prompts or reference images, including multiple-image inputs. Available controls may include format, resolution, duration, and sound. It also offers a Prompt Bank, AI Chat with optional image attachments, and local tools for History, Favorites, copying prompts, recreating generations, saving, sharing, or deleting results.\n\nAI features depend on third-party services, network connectivity, available model capabilities, and your subscription entitlements. We may update or discontinue particular features, settings, or models, subject to applicable law. Generation times, available resolutions, model behavior, and output quality can vary. The App does not provide a social network, public posting platform, or user-to-user messaging.\n\n## AI processing and limitations\n\nTo provide your requested features, the App sends relevant prompts, instructions, selected images, and AI Chat messages or context to external AI providers, including fal.ai and OpenAI. Generated results are returned to the App. We do not operate a proprietary backend for AI request storage. Provider processing, technical availability, and retention are governed by the providers’ applicable practices and terms, as further explained in our Privacy Policy.\n\nAI-generated outputs may contain errors, artifacts, unexpected elements, or similarities to existing material. They are not guaranteed to be factual, accurate, original, suitable for a particular purpose, non-infringing, or available for exclusive use. Do not rely on AI Chat for professional medical, legal, financial, emergency, or other high-stakes advice. You remain responsible for reviewing outputs before using or distributing them.\n\n## Your content, permissions, and generated results\n\nYou retain any rights you already hold in the prompts, images, and other materials you submit (“Input”). You must have all rights, consents, and permissions needed to upload or process the Input, including where it depicts identifiable people or uses third-party intellectual property.\n\nYou authorize the Operator and the relevant service providers, only as reasonably necessary to deliver the features you request, to transmit, process, host, adapt, and generate results from your Input. This permission is subject to the Privacy Policy and applicable provider terms. The legal status, copyright eligibility, and permissible commercial use of AI-generated outputs may depend on applicable law, third-party rights, and provider terms; we do not guarantee exclusive ownership or intellectual-property protection for generated results.\n\nYou may save or share outputs using the App’s available export functions, subject to these Terms, the rights of others, and the terms of any destination service. You are responsible for anything you choose to publish or share outside the App.\n\n## Acceptable use\n\nYou agree not to use the App to create, upload, request, or distribute content that:\n\n- Is unlawful; exploits or endangers children; is sexually explicit or intended to bypass the App’s restriction on 18+ generation; or promotes violence or threats.\n- Infringes another person’s intellectual property, privacy, publicity rights, or confidentiality, including unauthorized impersonation or deceptive use of a person’s likeness.\n- Harasses, defames, discriminates against, or otherwise unlawfully harms others, or is designed for fraud, deception, or malicious activity.\n- Attempts to bypass security, usage restrictions, subscription entitlements, content restrictions, or technical safeguards, or disrupts our providers or services.\n\nYou may not reverse engineer the App except where applicable law expressly permits, or use automated means to abuse, overload, or interfere with the service. We may restrict access to features or take appropriate action in response to misuse, consistent with applicable law.\n\n## Subscriptions, billing, and cancellations\n\nSome features require a paid, automatically renewing subscription offered through Apple’s in-app purchase system. Applicable prices, billing periods, feature access, and any trial or promotional terms are shown in the App Store purchase flow before confirmation. Apple processes payments; Apphud helps manage subscription status and entitlements. Subscription availability and offers may differ by region.\n\nUnless you cancel before the renewal date under Apple’s applicable purchase terms, a subscription may renew automatically and Apple may charge your selected payment method. You can manage or cancel subscriptions in your Apple Account subscription settings; deleting the App does not cancel a subscription. If a free trial is offered, the trial and conversion rules disclosed in the purchase flow will apply. Refunds are handled through Apple, subject to mandatory consumer rights and applicable law.\n\nIf a paid entitlement is not recognized, use the App’s available restore-purchases function or contact support. We may need limited transaction information to investigate an entitlement issue, but we do not receive your complete payment-card details.\n\n## Local storage, deletion, and privacy\n\nHistory, Favorites, and certain other settings are stored locally on your device. Where available, the App lets you delete individual results or history. Deleting local records does not necessarily remove copies saved to Photos, exported to other services, or already processed or retained by AI providers. We cannot guarantee deletion from third-party systems merely because an item was removed in the App.\n\nOur Privacy Policy explains the categories of data involved, the use of AI providers and Apphud, possible external retention, and your available privacy choices. You should review that Policy before submitting personal or sensitive information.\n\n## Intellectual property and authorized branding\n\nThe App’s software, interface, design, and other elements (excluding your own Input and third-party materials) are protected by applicable intellectual-property laws and are licensed to you for personal use in accordance with these Terms and the applicable Apple platform rules. You receive a limited, revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to use the App as permitted by law.\n\nHIGGSFIELD and associated marks belong to their respective rights holders and are used in connection with this App under a signed brand authorization agreement. The App is independently operated by Felix Lindner. The authorization to use the brand does not mean that Higgsfield Inc. is the publisher or contracting party for your use of this App. Other company names and marks, including service-provider marks, remain the property of their owners.\n\n## Disclaimers and responsibility\n\nTo the extent permitted by applicable law, the App and AI-generated features are provided on an “as available” basis. We do not guarantee uninterrupted access, a particular output, accuracy, uniqueness, completeness, or that content will be suitable for every use. Third-party service interruptions and model changes may affect the App.\n\nNothing in these Terms excludes or restricts rights or remedies that cannot legally be excluded, including mandatory consumer protections, statutory warranty rights, or liability for intentional misconduct, gross negligence, or personal injury where the law prohibits limitation. Any limitation of liability applies only to the extent permitted under the law that governs your claim.\n\n## Changes, termination, and applicable law\n\nWe may revise these Terms from time to time. Material changes will be communicated by an appropriate method where required. Continued use after lawful notice of amended Terms indicates acceptance only to the extent permitted by applicable law. You may stop using the App at any time and manage subscriptions separately through Apple.\n\nThese Terms are governed by German law, without depriving consumers in other countries of mandatory protections available under the laws of their habitual residence. Any dispute-resolution or court provisions are subject to mandatory consumer jurisdiction rules. If a provision is unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue in effect to the extent permitted by law.\n\n## Contact\n\nFor questions about these Terms, service availability, or subscription access, contact:\n\nFelix Lindner\nPrierosser Str. 45, 12357 Berlin, Germany\nEmail: felix@lindnerapp.click";

